  "prompt": "Use case: illustration-story. Asset type: Japanese elementary vocabulary illustrations, sheet 35. Edit the provided 2048x2048 template, painting ONLY inside its sixteen white panels. Every single panel MUST have identical width and height. All horizontal lines must be EXACTLY at 0%,25%,50%,75%,100%, not based on artwork. Keep precisely the 4x4 equal grid and 5 continuous pure magenta #ff00ff lines in each direction, including outer frame. Preserve line position, width and full canvas. Each panel is an independent clear gentle picture-book illustration as isolated vignettes on a pure white background, large and easily understood. Never use magenta for illustration. Avoid all pink, purple and neon colors in artwork, objects, decorations, lighting and shadows. Use warm orange, red, yellow, green, blue and neutral colors. No pink/purple concert lights. Nothing crosses the grid. No text, letters, numbers, labels, symbols resembling writing or watermarks. For abstract words show a concrete situation illustrating the meaning. Diverse natural children and adults, no stereotypes. Correct anatomy and objects. Panels in strict row-major order (left to right, top to bottom):\n1. 胸部 — 体の胸に当たる部分。\n2. 疑問符 — 問い掛けなどを表す「？」の記号。\n3. 逆向き — 基準の向きと反対の方向。\n4. ギャラリー — 美術作品などを展示する場所。\n5. 行儀 — 人前での振る舞いや態度。\n6. 行列 — 人などが順に並んだ列。\n7. 空気圧 — 空気が物を押す力の大きさ。\n8. 空中 — 地面から離れた空気の中。\n9. 草刈り — 伸びた草を刈ること。\n10. 草取り — 畑などの不要な草を抜き取ること。\n11. 草原 — 草が広く生えている場所。\n12. 屑籠 — 紙くずなどを入れるかご。\n13. 口コミ — 人から人へ話して情報が伝わること。\n14. 靴音 — 靴を履いて歩くときに出る音。\n15. 靴底 — 靴の地面に触れる底の部分。\n16. 靴紐 — 靴を足に合うように結ぶひも。\nSafety and clarity: Vehicles must be driven only by unmistakable adults, never children. Industrial machinery and knives are used by adults. Do not put a child in a car driver's seat. Keep artwork separated by the measured template grid.\nDo not add numerical claims, prices, quantities, currency denominations, calorie values or stroke-order numbers unless explicitly required by the target word. Mathematical concepts 